      "time": "2-6 April 1453",
      "durationSec": 8,
      "narration": "Mehmed II encamps before the Theodosian Walls with perhaps 50,000-80,000 men; his tent stands opposite the Mesoteichion where the walls dip into the Lycus valley. Constantine XI posts his thin garrison along 5.7 km of walls, with Giustiniani's Genoese on the land walls and the Golden Horn closed by a chain.",
